The Starglance logo

Copyright (c) 2026 Brad Quillen. All rights reserved, except as below.

The MIT license in this repository's LICENSE file covers Starglance's code and docs. It does
not cover the Starglance logo (the wings: a star in a diamond between two sets of wings) or
the artwork made from it. That is:

- every image in this brand/ folder (masters/, discord/, site/);
- the logo wherever else it appears in the repository: site/public/logo.svg,
  site/public/logo-light.svg, site/public/favicon.svg, the drawing in
  web/src/components/Logo.svelte, the favicon in web/index.html, and the icon that
  draw_icon in agent/starglance/app.py draws for starglance.exe and the tray.

The code in those files, brand/brand-export.cjs included, is MIT like the rest; the
drawing it makes is not.

You may, without asking:

- use the logo to refer to Starglance: in an article, a video, a review, a link to the
  project, or a post in its community;
- keep it in copies of Starglance built from this repository's code, and in a fork while
  you work on changes meant to come back to this project.

You may not, without permission:

- use the logo, or anything like it, on a modified version you distribute, or on another
  product or service, in a way that suggests it is Starglance or is made or endorsed by
  Starglance's maintainers. Before you distribute a fork, give it its own name and logo;
- change the logo, or use it as part of another logo;
- sell the logo, or things with it on.

To ask for permission, open an issue at https://github.com/bradqui/starglance/issues.

The images use the fonts Chakra Petch and IBM Plex Sans, under the SIL Open Font License.
